# RoadAhead Workflow Rules

## Mandatory Branch Hygiene

Every new issue or task starts from latest `origin/main`. Never branch from another issue branch.

```bash
git fetch origin
git checkout main
git pull --ff-only origin main
git checkout -b issue/<ISSUE_NUMBER>-<short-slug>
# For no-issue tasks: chore/<short-slug> or docs/<short-slug>
```

If a branch was accidentally created from another issue branch, rebase onto `origin/main` before opening a PR. Push with `--force-with-lease`.

Before opening a PR, always run:

```bash
git fetch origin
git diff --stat origin/main...HEAD
git log --oneline origin/main..HEAD
```

## PR Requirements

Every PR body must include:

```
Branch hygiene:
- Started from latest origin/main: yes
- Diff checked with origin/main...HEAD: yes
- PR contains only current task / issue changes: yes
```

- Reference the issue number when one exists.
- For no-issue tasks state: `No issue — maintenance / workflow task`.
- PR body must cover: what changed, validation, boundary statement, branch hygiene block.
- One issue → one branch → one PR unless explicitly instructed otherwise.

## Product Boundaries

RoadAhead is a driver-awareness assistant. It is **not** a navigator, anti-radar, legal speed-limit authority, or safety-certified system.

Do not use: legal / fine / violation / capture / police / enforcement-certain / radar-detector wording anywhere in code, comments, UI, or docs.

- External event data is candidate input only; it is not RoadAhead product truth.
- Raw Datakam / OpenSpeedcam data must not be committed.
- Provider / API / network integration is forbidden unless explicitly requested.

## Canon Boundary

- Product Canon lives under `docs/product/areas/`.
- Do not edit Canon files unless explicitly requested.
- WIP fixtures, scenario defaults, and numeric tuning values are not Canon.
- No numeric value may be promoted to Canon by implementation or tests alone.

## Validation

For changes under `web/roadahead-emulator/`:

```bash
cd web/roadahead-emulator
npm run build
npm run scenario:sweep
```

Scenario sweep is WIP evidence only. For documentation-only changes, emulator build is not required.

## Scope Control

Implement only the current task. Do not perform unrelated refactors, broad UI redesigns, or add new dependencies without justification. Do not introduce provider / API / network / raw datasets / Android overlay work unless explicitly requested. When scope is ambiguous, stop and clarify before changing files.
